  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, by reason of Room 2's narrow and inadequate width, would give rise to substandard and inappropriate accommodation, incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers of this particular bedroom. The development is thereby contrary to Policies; D3 and D6 of the London Plan, CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5, DMD 6, and DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the siting of vulnerable residential accommodation at ground floor level within an area identified as being at risk of surface water flooding by the Environment Agency's latest National Assessment of Flood Risk (NAFRA2) modelling, and in the absence of sufficient evidence demonstrating that finished floor levels would be raised above the design flood level, fails to demonstrate that future occupiers would be adequately protected from flood risk for the lifetime of the development, and, that the development would be safe without increasing flood risk elsewhere. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), Policies CP21 and CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD59, DMD60, DMD61 and DMD62 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the National Planning Policy Framework (2026)."
  ],
